ZeD-GUI source-available licence
Version 1, October 28, 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 Hermit the Trog. All rights reserved except as granted below.

ZeD-GUI (also written ZeD.UI and ZeD-UI) is a mod for Project Zomboid. This
licence covers everything in this repository that is Hermit the Trog's own
work: the Lua code, the pixel art, the baked font textures, the item scripts,
the documents and the tools. "The mod" means the files the game loads, in
any version. "You" means anyone who gets a copy.

This is not an open-source licence. The code is public so that people can
read it, learn from it, build on it and help with it. Distributing the mod
itself stays with the maintainer, so that there is one place to get it, one
place to report problems, and one version to support.


1. What you may do

  a. Read, study and run the code, and keep private copies and private
     forks for that purpose.

  b. Make add-ons. An add-on is a separate mod that requires ZeD-GUI, calls
     what ZeD-GUI exposes, and does not include ZeD-GUI's files. You may
     publish add-ons anywhere, under any licence you like, and say that
     they are "for ZeD-GUI".

  c. Send changes back. Pull requests, patches, translations, bug reports
     and test scripts are welcome; section 4 says what happens to them.

  d. Run the mod on servers, including dedicated ones, and let the game
     hand it to players the way the game does that.

  e. Quote short parts of the code in reviews, guides, bug reports, videos
     and other commentary, with credit.


2. What you may not do

  a. Re-upload, mirror or repost the mod, or any version of it changed or
     unchanged, to the Steam Workshop, to any other mod site, or anywhere
     else. This includes renamed copies, "fixed" copies, translated copies
     and copies bundled into mod packs or server packs.

  b. Sell the mod, or put it behind a paywall, a subscription or a
     donation gate.

  c. Publish a mod that includes ZeD-GUI's files in part or in whole. Build
     an add-on instead (section 1b).

  d. Call your own work ZeD-GUI, ZeD.UI or ZeD-UI, or present it as the
     official mod. The name belongs to the maintainer. "For ZeD-GUI" is
     fine for add-ons.

  e. Remove or change the credits, this licence, or the third-party
     notices (section 6).

If you want to do something this section does not allow, ask. Permission
given in writing by the maintainer is good for the thing it names.


3. The mod is actively maintained

The place to get the mod is its Steam Workshop page. The place to report
problems is the pinned Bug reports discussion there. The place to read and
discuss the code is the GitHub repository. Changes land through those
places, not through copies elsewhere. That is the whole reason for
section 2.


4. Contributions

If you send a change and it is merged, you keep the copyright on what you
wrote, and you licence it to the project under these same terms. You also
agree that the maintainer may re-licence your contribution together with
the rest of the project, as section 5 may require. If you cannot agree to
that, say so when you send it and it will not be merged.


5. Adoption, if the project is abandoned

The project is meant to outlive any one maintainer.

  a. The project counts as abandoned when, for twelve months in a row,
     there has been no release and no reply from the maintainer at any of
     the contact points in section 3, after a reasonable attempt to reach
     them there.

  b. If the maintainer has named a successor in the SUCCESSORS file in
     this repository, the successor becomes the maintainer, with every
     right this licence gives the maintainer, and the project continues
     under this licence.

  c. If no successor is named, or the named successor does not take it up
     within three months of the project becoming abandoned, this licence
     ends and the project passes to everyone under the GNU General Public
     License, version 3 or later. From then on anyone may carry it on,
     publish it and fork it under that licence, keeping the credits.

  d. A maintainer who comes back after section 5c has taken effect does
     not get the old terms back; the project stays under the GPL.


6. Third-party work

These are not Hermit the Trog's and have their own terms, which travel
with the files:

  - Fira Sans Condensed and Fira Mono (the baked font textures under
    42/media/fonts): copyright 2012-2015 The Mozilla Foundation and
    Telefonica S.A., licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
    https://openfontlicense.org

  - Project Zomboid, its Lua, its scripts and its art: copyright The Indie
    Stone. Parts of this mod follow the game's own Lua as every mod does,
    under The Indie Stone's terms for mods. Nothing in this licence covers
    the game's own content.

  - The makers of the mods ZeD-GUI does the job of are credited on the
    Workshop page. ZeD-GUI takes no donations; if you want to give
    something back, give it to them.

ZeD-GUI is a fan-made mod. It is not affiliated with The Indie Stone,
Apple or Microsoft. Its look is inspired by the operating systems of the
early 1990s; that is a style, not an endorsement of any brand.


7. No warranty

The mod and the code are provided as is, without warranty of any kind,
stated or implied, including fitness for any purpose. The maintainer and
the contributors are not liable for any loss or damage of any kind that
comes from using them, including lost saves, lost time and anything that
happens on a server. You use them at your own risk, and you are
responsible for complying with the terms of Steam and of the game.


8. Housekeeping

  - If a part of this licence turns out not to hold where you live, the
    rest still does.
  - Breaking section 2 ends your rights under section 1 until you put it
    right.
  - The maintainer may publish a later version of this licence. The
    version that ships with a copy of the mod is the one that applies to
    that copy.
